## Latent production bug found by CI and fixed upstream
Run 43992956445 (branch, before identity env) failed in internal/wormhole with "Committer identity unknown": `rebaseLocked` (git_sync.go:403+) ran plain `git rebase` without the `-c user.*` flags that `commitAtLocked` (git_sync.go:503) has, and `gitCommandEnv()` (git_sync.go:329) set no identity → push-recovery broken on hosts without a global git identity (bare CI runners, minimal containers). Fixed by Voyager in **2cc3274**: `gitCommandEnv()` now appends GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and GIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL (starfleetctl@localhost) — verified in the source at the tip (git_sync.go:337-339).

